config LICHEN_UX
	bool "LICHEN device UX (spec 19)"
	depends on LICHEN
	default y
	help
	  Device UX components from spec/19-device-ux.md. Compiles the pure,
	  host-testable engines (LED timing, etc.); GPIO/display backends are
	  individually selectable.

config LICHEN_UX_LED
	bool "Spec 19 §10 LED status language (led0 blink engine)"
	depends on LICHEN_UX
	default y
	help
	  Drive the device status LED with the fixed 6-state blink table from
	  spec 19 §10 (joined-idle off, joining, message-waiting, SOS, hold,
	  fault). Selects the GPIO backend that drives led0 via the HAL.
	  Boards set CONFIG_LICHEN_HAS_LEDS (which BUILD_ASSERTs an led0 alias);
	  targets with no LED (hal_led_get fails) degrade to a quiet no-op and
	  the driver does not schedule any periodic work.
